  beschreibung: Jupiter is the largest planet in the solar system and is made mostly
    of hydrogen and helium. Its bright and dark cloud bands are pulled in opposite
    directions by fast winds. The Great Red Spot is a huge storm that can be larger
    than Earth and has been observed for a long time. Jupiter's strong gravity shapes
    many moons, including the four large Galilean moons.
  planetSizeInfoText: Jupiter is the largest planet in the solar system. Its diameter
    is about eleven times Earth's diameter.
  orbitalDistanceInfoText: Jupiter orbits the Sun at about 5.20 AU, much farther
    away than the inner rocky planets.
  orbitalSpeedInfoText: Jupiter needs almost 12 Earth years to complete one orbit.
    Its orbit is large, so its movement appears slower in the model.
  axialTiltInfoText: Jupiter's axis is only slightly tilted, so its seasons are much
    less pronounced than Earth's.
  eccentricityInfoText: Jupiter's orbit is slightly elliptical, but not extreme.
    Overall, Jupiter remains far from the Sun.
  planetScaleInfoText: In a size comparison, Jupiter clearly dominates. It is the
    widest planet and looks enormous beside the rocky planets.
  gravityInfoText: Gravity at the cloud tops is more than twice as strong as on Earth.
  fakten:
  - Jupiter has no solid surface; what we see are cloud bands in its atmosphere.
  - Jupiter's bright and dark cloud bands move in opposite directions.
  - The Great Red Spot is a giant storm larger than Earth.
